# Scripts and commands

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` sections 8 and 9; details in `rules/editing-and-scripts.md`.

- Fail fast and return non-zero on failure.
- Idempotent: a second run changes nothing.
- Destructive operations get a dry-run mode that prints what would happen.
- Never print, log or commit a secret.
- Thin wrappers; logic in a testable script or module.
- Preserve encoding and line endings; check `git diff --stat` after editing.
- Long or quoting-heavy commands go into a script file run with a timeout; remote commands run a
  copied script instead of nested quotes.
- Tooling in the scripting language set in `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md`; shell wrappers stay thin.
- Files that are not UTF-8 are edited by a script that keeps their encoding and newlines.
- When exact bytes matter, capture output byte-safely instead of through shell redirection; know
  whether the shell writes a byte-order mark.
- A slow command is checked for progress before it is killed; locks and indexes in use are not
  deleted.
- Temporary workarounds carry a one-line comment naming the reason.
- Temporary files go to the system temp area and are removed after verification.
